 # L08 Storage Functional Companion
+
+## Companion 02: public Home scrolling
+
+The immutable native12 run of companion01 failed at boot10: the exact legacy
+Home tile existed uniquely, but its enabled/hittable readiness wait timed out.
+Its migration/load observation passed; this does not establish a broken app
+recovery path. The old driver never scrolled. With two damaged neighbors, the
+production Home shows a recovery warning and three ordered tiles, not the
+single-tile layout exercised earlier. No individual predicates or geometry were
+retained, so the precise reason for that earlier readiness failure is unknown.
+
+This revision adds only a copy-only tag to the real Home LazyColumn, up to eight
+real upward swipes on that exact list for the seven closed synthetic tile IDs,
+and bounded public presence/geometry diagnostics. A unique, enabled, hittable
+tile is still required before one and only one actual Resume tap. It adds no
+coordinate fallback, alternate selector, programmatic navigation or recovery
+shortcut. Ordinary fixture buttons and Retry/Discard keep their existing strict
+activation path. Storage, metadata, phase, image and cleanup checks are unchanged.
+
+This revision requires fresh tests and native evidence; native12 remains FAIL.
 
